' Location/context acquisition belongs to UC-006; other assessments consume the available context.
' These associations do not mandate a new provider request for each assessment.

' Optional handoff at the external-link action on candidate advice/detail.
' UC-021 remains complete without navigating; the arrow points from extension to base.
' norank affects layout only; UC-023 remains the optional extension and UC-021 the base.
UC023 .[norank].> UC021 : <<extend>>

' No include: confirmation, details, previews and validity/ranking remain behavior within their goals.
' No generalization: assisted/manual entry are alternatives of UC-007, not separate actor goals.



legend bottom
  Add Garment: image-assisted or imageless manual entry; user review/correction and confirmation establish authority.
  Saveable does not imply Recommendation-Ready. Garment removal preserves understandable history.
  Candidate evaluation: Wardrobe Multiplier and hypothetical previews; no new ownership or Wear Event.
  Device location/weather are optional; manual location remains available and reduced-context advice continues where evaluable.
  Feedback differs from reported wear. Available shopping links open only by user choice; purchases happen outside CapsuleAI.
endlegend

' Embedded-goal boundaries for later UC specifications:
' UC-004 covers request and completion of email reset; delivery failure never becomes completed reset.
' UC-005 includes initial setup, revision/removal of optional context, styles and common need priorities.
' UC-006 includes manual/device choice, optional weather retrieval, context change/retry and skip.
' UC-007 includes camera/gallery or imageless manual input, proposals where usable, correction, confirmation.
' UC-008 includes browse/search/filter/reset, garment detail, readiness and reported-use information.
' UC-009 requires confirmed supported edits; UC-010 requires deliberate removal confirmation.
' UC-011 includes current request occasion/style, valid owned choices and outfit detail/reasoning.
' Hard validity precedes personalized ranking inside UC-011; neither is a standalone use case.
' UC-012 preserves all non-shuffled constituents and request context; it creates no feedback or wear.
' UC-013 covers Like/Dislike, revision and clearing; UC-014 records a separate intentional Wear Event.
' UC-015 preserves original event-local history and labels removed garments in historical snapshots.
' UC-016/017 change a specific report, recomputing history/evidence without deleting outfits/garments.
' UC-018 shows reported utilization, not verified physical wear or fabricated no-history statistics.
' UC-019/020 retain assessment context and unavailable/insufficient/outdated/no-gap distinctions.
' UC-020 describes underserved capabilities before possible candidate characteristics.
' UC-021 includes candidate attributes, gap/utility reasons and credible optional commercial information.
' UC-022 includes Multiplier meaning/context, newly enabled previews and all five evaluation states.
' UC-022 evaluates a candidate from documented gap/advice; no candidate capture/import goal is introduced.
' Viewing candidates/previews or opening links creates no owned garment, verified purchase or Wear Event.
' Exactness, evidence aging and other domain constraints stay in Business Rules and later UC flows.
' ORQ-001 is resolved. OSQ-011..OSQ-014 retain their existing downstream gates; no parameter is invented.

' MVP FEAT coverage review: direct goals, embedded behavior, or intentionally cross-cutting.
' FEAT-AUTH-001 | direct | UC-001, UC-002, UC-003, UC-004 | Registration, login, logout and recovery; session continuity is embedded access behavior.
' FEAT-PROF-001 | direct | UC-005 | Set/update style, common need priorities and optional personal context; setup may be skipped and resumed.
' FEAT-PROF-002 | direct | UC-006 | Permission-based/manual location, retry and environmental context; used by recommendations and assessments.
' FEAT-AI-001 | embedded | UC-007 | Camera/gallery entry and AI preview are the assisted alternative, with manual fallback.
' FEAT-AI-002 | embedded | UC-007 | Imageless manual entry plus user review, correction and explicit confirmation.
' FEAT-GAR-001 | embedded | UC-007, UC-008, UC-009 | Rich descriptors, uncertainty, authority and evaluation-specific readiness.
' FEAT-WAR-001 | direct | UC-008 | Browse wardrobe and inspect garment details, including imageless entries.
' FEAT-WAR-002 | direct | UC-009, UC-010 | Confirmed edit/remove; removal affects active ownership without erasing history.
' FEAT-WAR-003 | embedded | UC-008 | Search, filter, inspect and reset browsing conditions.
' FEAT-OUT-001 | direct | UC-011 | Context selection and personalized valid outfit choices; hard validity precedes ranking.
' FEAT-OUT-002 | embedded | UC-011 | Inspect outfit garments, assessment context, compatibility and ranking reasons.
' FEAT-OUT-003 | direct | UC-012 | Replace one slot with a compatible owned garment while holding other constituents fixed.
' FEAT-PERS-001 | direct | UC-013 | Like/Dislike, revise/clear feedback; no implicit Wear Event.
' FEAT-PERS-002 | direct | UC-014, UC-015, UC-016, UC-017 | Intentional Wear recording and access/correction/removal of specific events.
' FEAT-PERS-003 | embedded | UC-011, UC-013, UC-014, UC-016, UC-017 | Behavioral ranking and evidence recalculation; not a separate calculation goal.
' FEAT-ANL-001 | direct | UC-015, UC-016, UC-017, UC-018 | Recorded history and utilization with effective correction/removal and historical snapshots.
' FEAT-ANL-002 | direct | UC-019 | Contextual Coverage Score and insufficient/outdated states.
' FEAT-GAP-001 | direct | UC-020 | Evidence-backed underserved capabilities, not compulsory products.
' FEAT-MULT-001 | embedded | UC-022 | Wardrobe Multiplier +N, context/limitations and newly enabled hypothetical outfit previews.
' FEAT-SHOP-001 | direct | UC-021, UC-022 | Candidate advice/details and utility review independent of commercial data.
' FEAT-SHOP-002 | direct | UC-023 | Optional external navigation and return/failure recovery; no transaction evidence.
' FEAT-MET-001 | cross-cutting | no standalone UC | Privacy-respecting measurement of specified interactions; no actor goal or analytics actor.
' FEAT-MET-001 sources: FR-MET-001..007; PRD Section 24. Measurement does not create a human/service actor.

@enduml
